=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The reported fault — Campus 1 (PC5–PC14, subnets 172.16.10.0/24, 172.16.20.0/24,
172.16.30.0/24) unable to reach Campus 2 (10.5.0.0/24, 10.6.0.0/24) — does not
exist in the live lab. All diagnostic evidence shows the network is fully
operational.

Router16's OSPF process is running normally: Router-ID 172.30.1.1, Area 0
backbone, two active interfaces, two Full adjacencies (one with mswitch0 via
bond0/10.2.2.x, one with router7 via eth2/172.30.1.x), SPF converged 12 times.
The 10.5.0.0/24 and 10.6.0.0/24 prefixes are correctly propagated via OSPF
through router7 → router8/router10 → router17 → sshswitch and are present in
the FIB of every router along the campus-to-campus path.

Data-plane verification confirms end-to-end reachability: pings from pc5
(172.16.10.5, VLAN10), pc9 (VLAN20), and pc12 (VLAN30) to both pc1
(10.5.0.1, VLAN5) and pc3 (10.6.0.3, VLAN6) return 0% packet loss in both
directions. Every OSPF speaker — router16, router7, router8, router10, router17,
mswitch0, and sshswitch — holds full adjacencies with all expected neighbours.

Root cause: There is no fault. The user's ticket is based on a false premise;
the inter-campus outage they describe does not exist.

Corrective action: Inform the helpdesk that the network is healthy. No
intervention on router16 or any other device is required. Ask the reporter to
re-test from the specific machines they believe are affected — the issue may have
been transient (a brief convergence event during a recent lab restart) and has
since self-resolved, or the test methodology may have been incorrect.
=== END ===
